# issue 0016/0017: the driver's key files. .status-client.key absorbed make's
# .qmake_previous, whose rule died with the client target in 0017 — the entry
# stays so an existing tree's leftover copy is not suddenly untracked.
# Every repo-root key file is `.status-<artifact>.key` (issue 0018 review, I2:
# the convention that makes `make clean`'s glob total) — the pattern covers the
# in-tree ones too (<buildDir>/.status-cmake.key).
.qmake_previous
# Used to track the simulated keycard mode changes via the USE_SIMULATED_KEYCARD build flag
.use_simulated_keycard_previous
.status-*.key
# Not anchored: an older tree may still carry a copy of the libsds key — under
# its pre-0018 name, and inside .statusgo-build/ or (worse) vendor/status-go/,
# where buildLibsds used to write it.
.libsds.key
*.qm

